        answer: "Most recent episodes improve meaningfully in 2 to 6 weeks. The Lancet Low Back Pain Series describes a pattern of rapid early improvement followed by a slower tail, with many people experiencing some residual or recurring symptoms. Recurrence does not mean your back is getting worse. It usually reflects load, sleep, stress, and training history more than structural change."
