        findings: "Exercise is the mainstay of rehabilitation after ACL reconstruction, with modalities as an early add-on when pain, swelling or limited knee motion hold exercise back. Return to running and return to training are the key milestones, but the guideline found no evidence on which criteria should decide progression or discharge, and it rated the certainty for most parts of rehabilitation as very low, so most of its recommendations rest on expert agreement. Rehabilitation before surgery might improve knee motion and quadriceps strength afterwards.",
        relevance: "Gives a current framework for rehabilitation after ACL reconstruction, built largely on expert agreement. Progress is judged on how the knee is doing as well as time since surgery, because the graft needs a minimum time to heal and no single set of criteria has been shown to be best",
